  "body": "Update the 41 shipped `.mch` files that place `head` directly under `base` so `MachineTree` reports true tool-side and table-side axes.\n\n## Context\n`crates/post/src/machine/tree.rs` (`MachineTree`) marks a linear or rotary axis as `MovingSide::Tool` only when it is an ancestor of a `head` part. On `upstream/main` (`a1c57b475`), 8 of 50 shipped `.mch` files nest `head` under a driven axis (`agiecut-classic-2s`, `doosan-dnm`, `doosan-dnm-3axis`, `emco-vmc-200`, `fehlmann-picomax55`, `millturn`, `sinker-edm`, `tilthead`). The other 41 file-form `.mch` files place `head` directly under `base` beside the axis chain, so every axis reads as `MovingSide::Table`.\n\n## Scope\n- Re-nest the `kinematics.default.parts` tree in those 41 shipped `.mch` files to match each physical machine (for example, `base -> Y -> X -> table` and `base -> Z -> head` on a C-frame VMC, or `base -> Y -> X -> Z -> head` on a gantry router).\n- Keep `parse_mch`, `mirror()`, `script_props()`, and `crates/app/src/machine/validate.rs` output unchanged for every machine.\n- Update the style note in `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` so new `.mch` files nest `head` under its moving axes instead of beside the axes.\n- Add library tests in `crates/post` or `crates/app` that check `MovingSide::Tool` and `MovingSide::Table` on representative C-frame mills, gantry routers, lathes, and wire EDMs.\n\n## Done means\n`MachineTree` reports the physical `MovingSide::Tool` and `MovingSide::Table` axes for every shipped file-form `.mch` file, `assets/machines/AGENTS.md` documents the nesting rule, and `parse_mch`, `mirror()`, and `machine_library` tests pass with zero regression.\n\nPart of #3239\n",
